@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `hvac-nouns`
IMPORT `hvac-fees-regs`
IMPORT `hvac-tests-calendars`

-- hvac-tests-fees.l4 -- the fee for each service under each vintage, and regulations 3, 4, 5.
--
-- Every expected value in the first section is taken from the source text it cites, not
-- from the code.  The index values in the regulation 3 section are HYPOTHETICAL: the sources
-- contain no index value, so these tests check the arithmetic and the rounding reading, not
-- any real update.  Nothing here asserts a fee for a day after 31 December 2025.

§ `Reg 2: the fee for each service under each vintage`

-- Theory exam.  Draft 2(א) 273; as made: no theory exam; as amended 2(א1) 158.
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` Draft `for` `a theory exam` EQUALS JUST 273
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` `As made` `for` `a theory exam` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` `As amended` `for` `a theory exam` EQUALS JUST 158

-- Practical exam.  Draft 2(ב) 194; as made 2(א) 194; as amended 2(א) 194.
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` Draft `for` `a practical exam` EQUALS JUST 194
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` `As made` `for` `a practical exam` EQUALS JUST 194
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` `As amended` `for` `a practical exam` EQUALS JUST 194

-- Objection on a theory exam score.  Draft 2(ג) 40; as made: none; as amended 2(ב) 40.
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` Draft `for` `an objection to a theory exam score` EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` `As made` `for` `an objection to a theory exam score` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` `As amended` `for` `an objection to a theory exam score` EQUALS JUST 40

-- Objection on a practical exam score.  Draft 2(ג) 40; as made 2(ב) 40; as amended: SILENT.
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` Draft `for` `an objection to a practical exam score` EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` `As made` `for` `an objection to a practical exam score` EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` `As amended` `for` `an objection to a practical exam score` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Applying for a licence or its renewal.  Draft 2(ד) 284; the regulations as made charge
-- for receiving the licence instead.
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` Draft `for` `an application for a licence or its renewal` EQUALS JUST 284
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` `As made` `for` `an application for a licence or its renewal` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` `As amended` `for` `an application for a licence or its renewal` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Receiving a licence or its renewal.  As made 2(ג) 284; as amended 2(ג) 284; draft: none.
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` Draft `for` `receiving a licence or its renewal` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` `As made` `for` `receiving a licence or its renewal` EQUALS JUST 284
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` `As amended` `for` `receiving a licence or its renewal` EQUALS JUST 284

-- Request for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or its renewal.  Draft 2(ה) 398;
-- as made 2(ד) 398; as amended 2(ד) 398.
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` Draft `for` `a request for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or its renewal` EQUALS JUST 398
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` `As made` `for` `a request for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or its renewal` EQUALS JUST 398
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` `As amended` `for` `a request for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or its renewal` EQUALS JUST 398

-- A refresher training under section 17.  Section 59 of the Law lets the Minister set a fee;
-- no vintage sets one.
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` Draft `for` `a refresher training under section 17` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` `As made` `for` `a refresher training under section 17` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the fee prescribed under` `As amended` `for` `a refresher training under section 17` EQUALS NOTHING

-- The objection fee is per objection ("בעד כל השגה"): three objections cost 120, and the
-- as-amended practical objection stays silent however many there are.
#ASSERT `the total fee prescribed under` `As made` `for` 3 `of` `an objection to a practical exam score` EQUALS JUST 120
#ASSERT `the total fee prescribed under` `As amended` `for` 3 `of` `an objection to a theory exam score` EQUALS JUST 120
#ASSERT `the total fee prescribed under` `As amended` `for` 3 `of` `an objection to a practical exam score` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 1: the exams the vintage defines`

#ASSERT `the exams that regulation 1 defines under` Draft EQUALS (LIST `Theory exam`, `Practical exam`)
#ASSERT `the exams that regulation 1 defines under` `As made` EQUALS (LIST `Practical exam`)
#ASSERT `the exams that regulation 1 defines under` `As amended` EQUALS (LIST `Theory exam`, `Practical exam`)

§ `Reg 3: updating the fees (hypothetical index values)`

-- HYPOTHETICAL values: 100 in the month before commencement, 101.2 in November 2025,
-- and 101.2 times 1.012 in November 2026.  Real values are not in the sources.
`a hypothetical index series` MEANS
    `Index series` WITH
        `published in the month before the regulations commenced` IS 100
        `published in the Novembers` IS LIST
            (`Index reading` WITH `the year of the November` IS 2025, `the index published then` IS 101.2)
          , (`Index reading` WITH `the year of the November` IS 2026, `the index published then` IS 102.4144)

-- The first update day after commencement (16 July 2025) is 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT `the first update day after the regulations commenced` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1

-- The base index for 2026 is the index of the month before commencement; for 2027 it is
-- the November 2025 index ("המדד שפורסם בחודש נובמבר שקדם ליום העדכון הקודם").
#ASSERT `the base index for the update on 1 January of` 2026 `in` `a hypothetical index series` EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the base index for the update on 1 January of` 2027 `in` `a hypothetical index series` EQUALS 101.2

-- 194 x 101.2 / 100 = 196.328, to the nearest whole new shekel 196.
#ASSERT `the amount` 194 `after the update of 1 January` 2026 `by` `a hypothetical index series` EQUALS 196

-- The step compounds: 40 x 101.2/100 = 40.48 rounds to 40; then 40 x 102.4144/101.2 = 40.48
-- rounds to 40.  Applying the cumulative ratio to the ORIGINAL 40 would give 40.97, i.e. 41:
-- the two readings of "the amounts specified in regulation 2" differ here (fork F-R3).
#ASSERT `the amount` 40 `after the update of 1 January` 2026 `by` `a hypothetical index series` EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `the amount` 40 `after the update of 1 January` 2027 `by` `a hypothetical index series` EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest whole new shekel` ((40 TIMES 102.4144) DIVIDED BY 100) EQUALS 41

-- An exact half is not covered by "the nearest": 50 x 101/100 = 50.5.
#ASSERT REFUSED `rounded to the nearest whole new shekel` 50.5
#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest whole new shekel` 50.49 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest whole new shekel` 50.51 EQUALS 51

-- Regulation 3(b): the duty to publish, with no time stated, stands until performed.
#TRACE `regulation 3(b): the Director General shall publish regulation 2 as updated` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
#TRACE `regulation 3(b): the Director General shall publish regulation 2 as updated` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Director General of the Ministry of Labour` DOES `publish in Reshumot the text of regulation 2 as changed by the update` AT 30

-- A November the series does not hold refuses; no index is invented.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the index published in the November of` 2030 `in` `a hypothetical index series`

§ `Reg 4: payment of the fee as a condition`

-- As made: a practical exam has a fee (194), so payment in full is a condition.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 makes full payment a condition of` `a practical exam` `under` `As made`
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 permits` `a practical exam` `under` `As made` `given payment in full is` FALSE
#ASSERT `regulation 4 permits` `a practical exam` `under` `As made` `given payment in full is` TRUE

-- As made: no theory exam fee is set, so there is nothing for reg 4 to condition.
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 makes full payment a condition of` `a theory exam` `under` `As made`
#ASSERT `regulation 4 permits` `a theory exam` `under` `As made` `given payment in full is` FALSE

-- As amended: the theory exam now has a fee, so the condition bites; but a practical
-- objection has none, so it can be filed unpaid.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 makes full payment a condition of` `a theory exam` `under` `As amended`
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 permits` `a theory exam` `under` `As amended` `given payment in full is` FALSE
#ASSERT `regulation 4 permits` `an objection to a practical exam score` `under` `As amended` `given payment in full is` FALSE

-- A licence and a temporary licence are covered; a refresher training is not.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 makes full payment a condition of` `receiving a licence or its renewal` `under` `As made`
#ASSERT `regulation 4 makes full payment a condition of` `a request for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or its renewal` `under` `As amended`
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 covers a service of the kind` `a refresher training under section 17`

-- Draft: reg 4 is not shown; encoded from the panel's gloss for exams only, refused elsewhere.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 makes full payment a condition of` `a theory exam` `under` Draft
#ASSERT `regulation 4 makes full payment a condition of` `a practical exam` `under` Draft
#ASSERT REFUSED `regulation 4 makes full payment a condition of` `receiving a licence or its renewal` `under` Draft
#ASSERT REFUSED `regulation 4 makes full payment a condition of` `an objection to a theory exam score` `under` Draft

§ `Reg 5: commencement, and which vintage was in force`

#ASSERT `the day the principal regulations commenced` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
#ASSERT `the principal regulations commenced, under` `As made` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
#ASSERT `the principal regulations commenced, under` `As amended` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
#ASSERT REFUSED `the principal regulations commenced, under` Draft

-- Reg 5 is "7 ימים מיום פרסומן", seven days from the publication on 9 July 2025.  Interpretation Law
-- s 10(a): the day of publication is not counted, so the period runs 10 to 16 July and ends on 16
-- July, the commencement day (fork F-R5, F-C3).  Counting 9 July as the first day (15 July) is
-- asserted, and fails, in hvac-tests-red.l4.
-- 16 July 2025 was a Wednesday, so s 10(c), applied to a commencement day, moves it under neither
-- calendar (fork F-X3).
#ASSERT (`the day the principal regulations commenced, if s 10(c) applied to a commencement day, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Saturdays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
#ASSERT (`the day the principal regulations commenced, if s 10(c) applied to a commencement day, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16

-- The amendment, Kovetz HaTakanot 12383, has no commencement provision.  Interpretation Ordinance
-- s 17: regulations of legislative effect begin to bind "ביום פרסומן, אם אין הוראה אחרת בענין זה"
-- (on the day of their publication, if there is no other provision), and it was published on 4 May
-- 2026.  So it commenced on 4 May 2026 (fork F-N1).  (Expectation moved: REFUSED in the first run.)
#ASSERT `the day the 5786 amendment commenced` EQUALS YMD 2026 5 4

-- Before 16 July 2025 no fee regulations were in force; from then until the amendment commenced,
-- the regulations as made; from 4 May 2026, as amended.  (The 4 May 2026 expectation moved:
-- REFUSED in the first run.)
#ASSERT `the vintage in force on` (YMD 2025 7 15) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the vintage in force on` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS JUST `As made`
#ASSERT `the vintage in force on` (YMD 2026 5 3) EQUALS JUST `As made`
#ASSERT `the vintage in force on` (YMD 2026 5 4) EQUALS JUST `As amended`
#ASSERT `the vintage in force on` (YMD 2026 12 31) EQUALS JUST `As amended`

-- If the caller supplies when the amendment commenced, the vintage is determinate.
#ASSERT `the vintage in force on` (YMD 2026 5 10) `if the amendment commenced on` (YMD 2026 5 4) EQUALS JUST `As amended`
#ASSERT `the vintage in force on` (YMD 2026 5 3) `if the amendment commenced on` (YMD 2026 5 4) EQUALS JUST `As made`

-- The fee payable on a day: the printed amount before the first update day, nothing the
-- sources can answer afterwards.
#ASSERT `the fee payable on` (YMD 2025 8 1) `for` `a practical exam` EQUALS JUST 194
#ASSERT `the fee payable on` (YMD 2025 12 31) `for` `receiving a licence or its renewal` EQUALS JUST 284
#ASSERT `the fee payable on` (YMD 2025 8 1) `for` `a theory exam` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT REFUSED `the fee payable on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `for` `a practical exam`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the fee payable on` (YMD 2025 7 1) `for` `a practical exam`
-- From 4 May 2026 the amended vintage is the one in force, and the printed amount is still not an
-- answer: reg 3 updated it on 1 January 2026 and the sources have no index value.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the fee payable on` (YMD 2026 5 10) `for` `a theory exam`
